urname>Edskes</surname><given-names>H.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>V.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wickner</surname><given-names>R.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The [URE3] prion is an aggregated form of Ure2p that can be cured by overexpression of Ure2p fragments</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA</source><volume>96</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>1498</fpage><lpage>1503</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9990052</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Fernandez-Bellotetal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fernandez-Bellot</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Guillemet</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cullin</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The yeast prion [URE3] can be greatly induced by a functional mutated URE2 allele</article-title><source>EMBO J.</source><volume>19</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>3215</fpage><lpage>3222</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10880435</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Gloveretal1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glover</surname><given-names>J.R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kowal</surname><given-names>A.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shirmer</surname><given-names>E.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Patino</surname><given-names>M.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>J.-J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindquist</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Self-seeded fibers formed by Sup35, the protein determinant of [<italic>PSI</italic>+], a heritable prion-like factor of <italic>S. cerevisiae</italic></article-title><source>Cell.</source><volume>89</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>811</fpage><lpage>819</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9182769</pub-id></citation></ref><re